setting up python 

https://francesco-onorati.medium.com/another-clean-python-setup-on-macos-guide-cf82c8be6865

USE STEPS...

pyenv virtualenv 3.11.8 myproject
pyenv activate myproject
cd myproject

poetry init
poetry add numpy pandas scikit-learn
poetry shell

pyenv deactivate

poetry add ipykernel
poetry run python -m ipykernel install --user --name=myproject --display-name "Python (myproject)"

Option A: VS Code
Open your project folder in VS Code.
Open Command Palette (Cmd+Shift+P) → Python: Select Interpreter → choose Python (myproject).
When you open a Jupyter notebook, select the Python (myproject) kernel.